ok anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5
factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 3 problems
  The reel_script and caption say the 700+ devotees came from Lalapettai, Krishnarayapuram and Mayanur, but the article says these devotees came from many areas, and the 700+ figure is tied to the Karupathur temple where the Kaveri bathing took place. The reel_script also says 700+ devotees at Karupathur only in the slides spec, so the attribution of the area list is mixed.
  The caption's Karupathur paragraph says devotees bathed in the Kaveri and wore garlands from the temple priest at 6 am, which is supported, but the reel_script sentence 'கருப்பத்தூர் கோவிலில் காலை 6 மணி முதல் பக்தர்கள் காவிரி ஆற்றில் குளித்து மாலை அணிந்தனர்' merges the bathing detail with the garland detail in a way that is acceptable, yet the slides_spec line 'காலை 6 மணி முதல் பக்தர்கள் கூடினர்' adds 'gathered', which is not stated in the article.
  The reel_script omits the important fact that devotees observe the fast from the start of Karthigai and that the Karur temple event happened early morning on the day the month began; the article's core facts about who did what are mostly present, but the reel_script says Sabarimala 'நடை திறக்கப்பட்டது நேற்று முன்தினம்' while the article does not clearly tie the Sabarimala opening to the Karur event, making the mixed-fact sentence unclear.
